From ece00a1d5171a5e037adfa935d2124734466f93f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philipp Schmitt <philipp@schmitt.co>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:24:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] launcher: weather line under the date, from a TV setting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Shows the global setting tvhome_weather (for example "☁ 12°") as a line
under the date, right of the clock. The date column is bottom-aligned, so
the date moves up by one line while a weather line is set. The line is
hidden when the setting is empty, and when tvhome_weather_at (epoch seconds,
optional) is older than three hours.

The launcher stays free of the INTERNET permission: something else on the
network writes the setting, for example Home Assistant through adb:

  settings put global tvhome_weather "☁ 12°"
  settings put global tvhome_weather_at $(date +%s)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JUnNRFEuDp94xcJGJ5R29o
